# The endoscope monitor's basic interaction scenario (#320, ADR-020).
#
# One directive per line, matching the .medui component-body convention. Events queue; `advance`
# consumes the queued batch as one accepted batch and runs that many application updates; an
# `expect` after an `advance` checks the state that advance settled (ADR-018 clause 6: state bound
# after the batch). Everything the replay checks here is a governed fact - a FieldEditor value, a
# PressLatch state, an ActionTrace, a FrameStats counter - or a demonstration reading.

scenario endoscope-monitor-basics
screen endoscope-monitor
version 1
clock 2026-09-09 08:00:00
sample 60
requirement REQ-EM-002 REQ-EM-003

# --- frame 1: an empty batch settles the initial state ---
advance
expect clock 08:00:01
expect state classifier-state 0
expect reading insufflation-pressure 120
expect latch -
expect overflow false

# --- frame 2: focus the patient-id field and type two accepted, two refused characters ---
key Commit
text A
text 7
text a
text -
advance
expect field "A7"
expect refused 2

# --- frame 3: press the ordinary freeze Button (one batch, two events) ---
pointer down freeze
pointer up freeze
advance
expect button freeze FREEZE
expect latch -
capture freeze-pressed

# --- frame 4: press the emergency-halt critical control ---
pointer down emergency-halt
pointer up emergency-halt
advance
expect action emergency-halt TriggerHalt REQ-EM-003
capture halt-activated

# --- advance far enough that the demonstration classifier steps to its next state ---
advance 27
expect state classifier-state 1
expect clock 08:00:31
